Z||000003||fierosound||07-20-2000||12:07 AM||||WoHoo!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Looking foward to getting those Borlas.  My 3.4L is being balanced as we speak.  I've got all my other goodies: ported heads, roller rockers, roller cam & lifters, FOCOA coated headers, under-drive pulley, matched 3.4 DOHC injectors and more...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>I know alot of the guys think $420 is too expensive for a Borla stainless steel exhaust system. I think that is not a bad price for the BORLA system at all! If you compare the price of Borlas on other cars - prices range from $400 to over $1000!!!! Also, compare that to other stainless systems for the Fiero.<P>Check out the price of this stainless steel exhaust system from Fiero Heaven. <A HREF="http://www.fieroheaven.com/Exhaust.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroheaven.com/Exhaust.htm</A>  <P>RS Motorsports also has a stainless steel exhaust system for US$680. <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/</A>  <P>Of course, there's always the Ocelot exhaust from The Fiero Store and GM's stock exhaust system to choose from as well. I've looked through the Fiero Store catalog - stock cat back systems are $180, Ocelot aluminized pipe cat backs are $270. They aren't performance systems. <A HREF="http://www.secureleadercom.com/fierostore/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secureleadercom.com/fierostore/</A>  <P>I haven't heard anything further from Fiero Shop regarding his stainless exhaust system, and he never stated his expected price. <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A>  <P>At present, the Borla system is still the best priced of the stainless steel performance exhaust systems for the Fiero THAT I COULD FIND. Borla is a performance system with proven engineering - why re-invent the wheel??<P>See the system at: <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroparts.com</A>  <P>To order, email Tim at: tim@fieroparts.com<BR>You can phone Tim at: (207) 934-0103<P>||||reg||6
